Article 1 The People's Court shall accept the following trademark cases:
1. Administrative cases against the review decisions or adjudications made by the National Intellectual Property Administration;
2. Cases against other administrative acts concerning trademarks made by the National Intellectual Property Administration;
3. Cases of disputes over ownership of trademark rights;
4. Cases of disputes over infringement of trademark rights;
5. Cases of disputes over confirmation of non-infringement of trademark rights;
6. Cases of disputes over trademark right transfer contracts;
7. Cases of disputes over trademark licensing contracts;
8. Cases of disputes over trademark agency contracts;
9. Cases of applications for pre-litigation cessation of infringement of the exclusive right to use a registered trademark;
10. Cases of applications for cessation of infringement and damages liability with respect to the exclusive right to use a registered trademark;
11. Cases of applications for pre-litigation property preservation;
12. Cases of applications for pre-litigation evidence preservation;
13. Other trademark cases.
